/T (The humble woven mat has long been an integral part of rural life in India.  From Satyajit Ray's villages to Kerala's art films, it appears beneath conversations, shared meals and afternoon naps, evoking memories of childhood summers and the quiet rhythms of village life.  Here, we look at a few of India's rare and remarkable handwoven mats.)
