/T (Traditionally, production was organised at the household level. Men generally undertook the physically demanding work of harvesting bamboo from the forest and preparing the raw material by splitting the culms. Women were the principal weavers, making the lattice patterns that create the mirror effect. Children and elders often assisted by sorting, cleaning and preparing strips.Kannadippaya weaving is a collaborative family activity and an important means of passing knowledge between generations. )
