/Title (Wagguv mats are traditional Kashmiri floor mats made by weaving reed grass from ponds and waterways or from dried rice straw.  They are soft, eco-friendly, and keep homes warm in winter and cool in summer. The craft is about 300 years old.Traditionally, these mats were used in almost every mosque, shrine and Kashmiri home.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 131 0 R
/Next 301 0 R
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Title (Traditionally, production was organised at the household level. Men generally undertook the physically demanding work of harvesting bamboo from the forest and preparing the raw material by splitting the culms. Women were the principal weavers, making the lattice patterns that create the mirror effect. Children and elders often assisted by sorting, cleaning and preparing strips.Kannadippaya weaving is a collaborative family activity and an important means of passing knowledge between generations.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 302 0 R
/Next 132 0 R
>>
endobj
